      40      0.6197    0.0772                0.0767
     160      0.6200    0.0382                0.0384
     640      0.6200    0.0192                0.0192
PASS  U_hat is unbiased at every batch size
PASS  and its noise falls as 1/sqrt(n)   | std err 0.1534 at n=10 vs 0.0193 at n=640 (~8.0x, sqrt(64) = 8)

  best-of-12 on n=20: observed 0.7528  but its TRUE utility 0.5781  (inflated by +0.1747)
PASS  selecting the max on a small batch OVERSTATES its utility   | so a 'gain' measured on the same batch that selected it is not a gain — eq. 3's cell revisits this
